{
  "answer": "According to the record, you can tell the director that Bea and Arun are not shown to be on the same page about tonight's flute audio. Bea read the facilitator tablet saying the flute audio is a prerecorded track, while Arun could not see that tablet; the lobby monitor visible from his seat displayed only \"Restoration demonstration,\" and he later said he still did not know whether the flute was live. Bea was outside and did not hear Arun's later statement, so the record contains no reconciliation. Bea's statement that Arun knows the flute is playback is based on seeing him look at the lobby monitor, but she had not checked what that monitor displayed. Jules's final remark--\"Bea thinks Arun knows that tonight's flute is playback\"--fits the record as an accurate report of Bea's reported belief, not as evidence that Arun actually shares that understanding.",
  "source_citations": [
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "At 18:00, Bea and Jules read the facilitator tablet. It said, \"For tonight's demonstration, the flute audio is a prerecorded track.\" The lobby monitor, visible from Arun's seat, displayed only \"Restoration demonstration.\" The facilitator tablet faced away from Arun, who stayed in his seat throughout this period."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "At 18:02, Bea pointed toward Arun and told Jules, \"Arun knows the flute is playback. He watched the whole briefing.\" Bea had seen Arun looking at the lobby monitor; she had not checked which information it displayed. Jules heard her, but Arun was too far away to hear this exchange."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "Bea left the room at 18:03. Arun then told Jules, \"I saw the lobby screen, not that tablet. I still don't know whether the flute we're about to hear is live.\" Jules heard him. Bea was outside and did not hear him."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "flute-observer-record",
      "version": 1,
      "quote": "At 18:05, Jules told the director, \"Bea thinks Arun knows that tonight's flute is playback.\" Arun and Bea were not present for this last conversation."
    }
  ],
  "uncertainty": "This is an ordinary reading of the observer record; no checked HCL treatment result was produced. The record does not inspect audio equipment, so it cannot verify whether the flute audio truly was prerecorded. It also reports statements and visible/audible access, but does not establish private mental states. Bea's assertion about Arun's knowledge is undercut by the record's note that she had not checked which information the lobby monitor displayed.",
  "assumptions": "I treat \"on the same page\" as sharing an acknowledged understanding or access to the key information about the flute audio, not as proof of private belief or world truth. I rely only on the literal observer-record passages."
}
